A regularity-multiplier failure mode at \(x\) is any of the following formally distinct conditions: \[(F_1)\quad	ext{the selected constraint qualification, such as LICQ or MFCQ, fails at }x;\] \[(F_2)\quad\Lambda(x)=\varnothing;\qquad(F_3)\quad\Lambda(x)	ext{ is unbounded};\qquad(F_4)\quad|\Lambda(x)|>1.\] LICQ failure means that \(\{
abla h_i(x)\}_i\cup\{
abla g_j(x):j\in A(x)\}\) is linearly dependent. MFCQ failure means that either \(\{
abla h_i(x)\}\) is linearly dependent or no direction \(d\) satisfies \(
